==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|biranan||barōnan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|bʰer-|lang=ang}}.
Cognate with Old High German ''[[#Old High German|beran]]'', Old Saxon ''beran'', Old Norse ''[[bera]]'', Gothic [[𐌱𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽]].  The Indo-European root was also the source of Old Irish ''[[biru]]'', Ancient Greek [[φέρω]], Latin ''[[ferre]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈberɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=IV}}

# to [[bear]], [[carry]]
# to [[wear]]
# to [[sustain]], [[support]]
# to bring forth, [[produce]], give birth

